Recommends: playerctl,
            wtype
Description: userspace driver for the Logitech G510 keyboard
 Drives the parts of a Logitech G510 that the kernel leaves alone. The in-tree
 hid-lg-g15 driver already exposes the RGB backlight, the M-key LEDs and the
 G-keys as ordinary input and LED devices; this adds the 160x43 LCD, bindings
 for the eighteen G-keys and the five keys under the display, and macro
 recording and replay.
 .
 The agent runs as a systemd user unit rather than as root, because it types
 into the session and launches the user's applications. It reaches the
 keyboard through hidraw and the LED class, with access granted by the udev
 rules this package installs.
 .
 playerctl is used by the now-playing screen and wtype by bindings that type
 text on Wayland; both are optional and the features that need them are
 skipped when they are absent.
